WEBVTT

NOTE
Disc 1, Scene 13h: The Two Gardens Approach
Duration: 27 seconds
Context: Balamb Garden and Galbadia Garden move toward each other for battle. This is an unprecedented sight — two massive flying academies preparing for war.
For blind and low-vision players using screen readers.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A wide aerial view reveals two colossal structures approaching each other across an expanse of ocean and coastline. Balamb Garden appears first — a sleek, modern facility with white and blue architecture, clean lines, and a commanding presence. Its design is pristine and academic.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Galbadia Garden emerges into view from the opposite direction. Its red-brown military aesthetic contrasts sharply with Balamb's white and blue. The red fortress is larger, more heavily fortified, with bulkier armor plating and weapon installations visible across its exterior. Both facilities hover above the landscape below.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The two Gardens move inexorably toward each other. The gap between them narrows. This is an unprecedented sight in the world of Final Fantasy VIII — two entire floating academies, each capable of housing hundreds of students and military personnel, are preparing for direct combat. The scale is staggering.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Students mobilize on both structures. On Balamb Garden, SeeD members take up defensive positions, weapons ready. On Galbadia Garden, soldiers stand at attention, preparing for an assault. The two massive fortresses continue their inexorable approach, about to collide.